ERROR:  column "r" of versioned table "app.t" cannot be of type regdictionary, which names an object
DETAIL:  A rename changes such a value with no change of the row, and names differ between branches.
CREATE TABLE t (id int PRIMARY KEY, r regnamespace);
ERROR:  column "r" of versioned table "app.t" cannot be of type regnamespace, which names an object
DETAIL:  A rename changes such a value with no change of the row, and names differ between branches.
CREATE TABLE t (id int PRIMARY KEY, r regrole);
ERROR:  column "r" of versioned table "app.t" cannot be of type regrole, which names an object
DETAIL:  A rename changes such a value with no change of the row, and names differ between branches.
CREATE TABLE t (id int PRIMARY KEY, r regcollation);
ERROR:  column "r" of versioned table "app.t" cannot be of type regcollation, which names an object
DETAIL:  A rename changes such a value with no change of the row, and names differ between branches.
CREATE TABLE t (id int PRIMARY KEY, r regdatabase);
ERROR:  column "r" of versioned table "app.t" cannot be of type regdatabase, which names an object
DETAIL:  A rename changes such a value with no change of the row, and names differ between branches.
CREATE TABLE t (id int PRIMARY KEY, r aclitem);
ERROR:  column "r" of versioned table "app.t" cannot be of type aclitem, which names an object
DETAIL:  A rename changes such a value with no change of the row, and names differ between branches.
-- inside an array, a domain, a composite type, and those in each other
CREATE TABLE t (id int PRIMARY KEY, r regclass[]);
ERROR:  column "r" of versioned table "app.t" cannot be of type regclass[], which names an object
DETAIL:  A rename changes such a value with no change of the row, and names differ between branches.
CREATE DOMAIN app.names_a_class AS regclass;
CREATE TABLE t (id int PRIMARY KEY, r app.names_a_class);
ERROR:  column "r" of versioned table "app.t" cannot be of type names_a_class, which names an object
DETAIL:  A rename changes such a value with no change of the row, and names differ between branches.
CREATE TYPE app.holds_a_role AS (who regrole, n int);
CREATE TABLE t (id int PRIMARY KEY, r app.holds_a_role);
ERROR:  column "r" of versioned table "app.t" cannot be of type holds_a_role, which names an object
DETAIL:  A rename changes such a value with no change of the row, and names differ between branches.
CREATE TYPE app.holds_holder AS (inner_one app.holds_a_role);
CREATE TABLE t (id int PRIMARY KEY, r app.holds_holder[]);
ERROR:  column "r" of versioned table "app.t" cannot be of type holds_holder[], which names an object
DETAIL:  A rename changes such a value with no change of the row, and names differ between branches.
CREATE DOMAIN app.many_names AS app.names_a_class[];
CREATE TABLE t (id int PRIMARY KEY, r app.many_names);
ERROR:  column "r" of versioned table "app.t" cannot be of type many_names, which names an object
DETAIL:  A rename changes such a value with no change of the row, and names differ between branches.
CREATE TYPE app.class_range AS RANGE (SUBTYPE = regclass, SUBTYPE_OPCLASS = oid_ops);
CREATE TABLE t (id int PRIMARY KEY, r app.class_range);
ERROR:  column "r" of versioned table "app.t" cannot be of type class_range, which names an object
